abstract: >
  This project presents a modular command-line interface (CLI) pipeline for analyzing disease symptoms using patient profile data.
  The pipeline covers end-to-end stages of a machine learning workflow, including data loading, preprocessing, and exploratory data analysis (EDA),
  feature engineering, model training with hyperparameter tuning, and evaluation using performance metrics such as AUC, MCC, sensitivity, and specificity.

  The repository features a fully automated CI/CD pipeline using GitLab CI to ensure reproducibility, code linting, unit testing, and deployment.
  Results, artifacts, and visualizations are automatically generated and stored. The project is maintained as part of the Research Software Engineering Lab
  at TU Dresden and adheres to best practices in research software development, version control, and team collaboration.
